  "updatedAt": "2026-08-23T10:37:25.159Z",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef q_learning_update(Q: list, s: int, a: int, r: float, s_next: int, alpha: float, gamma: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    q_arr = np.array(Q, dtype=float)\n    td_target = r + gamma * np.max(q_arr[s_next])\n    q_arr[s, a] = q_arr[s, a] + alpha * (td_target - q_arr[s, a])\n    return np.round(q_arr, 6)\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
